Rather than all the other changes being made in the Concat implementation, why not just keep this simple and have it be:
```C#
IEnumerable<TSource> result = first.Concat(second);
foreach (IEnumerable<TSource> next in rest)
{
    result = result.Concat(next);
}
return result;
```
and have the rest of the concat implementation sort out optimizing the chaining?
